content.text:
The root cause is the search service going down. Its deployment reports zero available pods for the whole abnormal window, and it emits no spans there. Every `/hotels` request then fails at frontend with HTTP 500. Reservation and the idle geo and rate services are downstream effects, not faults. Output:

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, count(*) n, min(value) mn, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "search deployment available is 0 across all abnormal samples; normal baseline is 1."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search') AS abnormal_search_spans, (SELECT count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='search') AS normal_search_spans", "claim": "search emits zero spans in the abnormal window versus about 1100 in the normal window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "All 565 frontend calls to search.Search/Nearby error out in about 0.016 ms, i.e. immediate connection failure."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Every frontend HTTP /hotels request returns status 500 with Error status in the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, min(value) mn, max(value) mx, count(*) n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'search%' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "The search pod restart counter climbs to 8 in the abnormal window, above normal baseline of at most 3."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('search.Search/Nearby','HTTP /hotels') GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Frontend search calls and the /hotels HTTP requests both fail with 565 errors each, matching search's outage."}]}
  ]
}
```

